    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Don’t you get tired of making so many trips to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "beri"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " every day?” I asked Nakata Devi. The 75-year-old was drawing buckets of water, one after another, from the only source of water in the area—Khadero ki Dhani. It was one of the driest places in India. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "beri"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is a narrow-mouthed well that collects and stores rainwater. It stood about a kilometre away from Devi’s village."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“I do. This is my seventh round since this morning. But do I have a choice? We need water. The animals need to drink, too,” Devi said as she poured water into the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "troughs",
            "zh": "饮水槽"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " she had placed beside the "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "beri"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The cows and goats gathered around, and within seconds, the troughs were empty. I also wanted the cool, sweet "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "beri"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " water. It was 11 a.m., but the sun was already burning overhead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Devi was soon joined by other women from her village, all carrying water vessels."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Do men also come here to fetch water?” My question made them laugh."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Never. Only we do it,” said Monu Kanwar, 18."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My driver and local guide, a middle-aged man, quickly jumped in. “They have to go to work.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Kanwar shook her head slightly, but I caught it. She later told me that the men in the village never fetched water even when they were home. It had always been women’s work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As summer drew near, the water level in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "beri"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " would start to drop. How would they get through the long dry season? “We don’t bathe for 10 to 15 days, and don’t wash clothes for around 20 days,” said 55-year-old Dhuri Devi."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p10",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Life here was no doubt hard. But the women’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "calmness",
            "ref": "v-calmness"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " made it appear "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bearable",
            "ref": "v-bearable"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “I was 11 when, for the first and the last time, I used two buckets of water for a bath. My grandfather beat me,” said Kanwar. “That’s how "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "our habits"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "shaped",
            "ref": "v-shape"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ".”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
